I've prepared a fix for this in branch `mvanhorn:fix/session-start-hook-timing`.

The fix fires `SessionStart` hooks eagerly during session creation (right after `SessionConfigured` is emitted) instead of deferring them to the first turn. The hook outcome (`should_stop` + `additional_contexts`) is stored on `SessionState` and consumed by the first turn, preserving the existing context injection behavior while fixing the timing.

Key changes:

  * `hook_runtime.rs`: new `run_session_start_hooks_eager()` fires hooks at init time using `send_event_raw` (no `TurnContext` needed)
  * `hook_runtime.rs`: `run_pending_session_start_hooks()` checks for a stored eager outcome before falling back to deferred execution
  * `state/session.rs`: new `EagerSessionStartHookOutcome` type and field
  * `codex.rs`: session init calls eager hooks instead of setting `pending_session_start_source`

Builds cleanly with `cargo check -p codex-core`. Branch is at https://github.com/mvanhorn/codex/tree/fix/session-start-hook-timing

